chosen product: Spotify
- What I believe happens when I press the main button (The „play“-button): The song just starts playing
- What actually happens: connection to Spotify’s servers is established - song is streamed - there could be a short delay while the song buffers - license check runs (Premium/Free) - Playback position syncs - song is stored in your cache

chosen product: Gmail-App:
- What I believe happens when I press the main button (The „send E-mail“-button): The email gets sent
- What actually happens: email is first moved to Outbox folder - It’s then uploaded to the mail server -The server processes it and sends it through various mail servers to the recipient - there could be delays (slow servers, network unstable) - (email could fail: land in recipient’s spam folder, invalid address,..)


